    Header 4|Hard EOLs
    Text
      Text:
        JavaScript wakes up, decides your type at runtime.
        You gave a number, now it thinks it’s a string, fine.
        Undefined shows up like an uninvited guest.
        Null sits quiet, still fails every test.
        You debug for hours, turns out, missing semicolon, best.
    gap

